k. After a correction, explicitly review its explanation to collect reward. Finish the shift after all 15 decisions and review your three handover notes.","Bring your learning summary to class. Rewards are game progress, not evidence of independent clinical competence."],"sourceDocumentIds":["SRC_PLAN","SRC_SLIDES","SRC_HANDOUT"],"contentVersion":"ptd-minigame-focused-2026-10-09"},{"id":"R1","title":"Anatomy, ligaments and force direction","estimatedMinutes":4,"body":["The anterior and posterior ring form one linked structure.","Ligament disruption explains instability clues.","Mechanism suggests a pattern, not a definitive diagnosis.","Look beyond the pelvis; these percentages describe the supplied source cohort.","Source-reported hip dislocation is an orthopaedic urgency; escalate, do not reduce independently."],"sourceDocumentIds":["SRC_SLIDES","SRC_PLAN","SRC_HANDOUT"],"contentVersion":"ptd-minigame-focused-2026-10-09"},{"id":"R2","title":"ATLS, shock and resuscitation","estimatedMinutes":4,"body":["Class III is a teaching estimate; trends and response matter more than a bucket.","Prepare access, tests, blood and stabilization while escalating.","80% venous, 20% arterial in the source; angio addresses arteries, not venous bleeding.","State physiology, response, uncertainty and an urgent request.","Reassess physiology and capability before CT, while treatment continues.","No blind Foley with meatal bleeding: ask the senior/urology team for assessment.","Source-table recall only: confirm allergy, age/weight, renal function and local protocol before prescribing.","General surgery, orthopaedics and urology coordinate; double set-up is senior-led."],"sourceDocumentIds":["SRC_SLIDES","SRC_PLAN","SRC_HANDOUT"],"contentVersion":"ptd-minigame-focused-2026-10-09"},{"id":"R3","title":"Binder: placement and reassessment","estimatedMinutes":4,"body":["Prepare access, tests, blood and stabilization while escalating.","Greater trochanters; supported alignment, padding and skin checks.","Stabilization supports clot formation; it does not prove bleeding has stopped."],"sourceDocumentIds":["SRC_SLIDES","SRC_PLAN","SRC_HANDOUT"],"contentVersion":"ptd-minigame-focused-2026-10-09"},{"id":"R4","title":"AP, inlet/outlet, CT and stability clues","estimatedMinutes":4,"body":["Recall this source''s series; choose actual imaging with the trauma team.","Review hip congruence and both rings; the source case report is authoritative.","Inlet assesses AP displacement; outlet assesses vertical displacement.","Normal physiology is not proof of mechanical stability.","Reassess physiology and capability before CT, while treatment continues.","Source-reported hip dislocation is an orthopaedic urgency; escalate, do not reduce independently."],"sourceDocumentIds":["SRC_SLIDES","SRC_PLAN","SRC_HANDOUT"],"contentVersion":"ptd-minigame-focused-2026-10-09"},{"id":"R5","title":"Open injury, soft tissue and GU","estimatedMinutes":4,"body":["Protect dignity and consent. Meatal blood suggests GU injury; it does not confirm the diagnosis.","Open means communication with the fracture. Blood PR/PV raises suspicion, not certainty.","Source-table recall only: confirm allergy, age/weight, renal function and local protocol before prescribing.","General surgery, orthopaedics and urology coordinate; double set-up is senior-led."],"sourceDocumentIds":["SRC_SLIDES","SRC_PLAN","SRC_HANDOUT"],"contentVersion":"ptd-minigame-focused-2026-10-09"},{"id":"R6","title":"Referral and senior haemorrhage planning","estimatedMinutes":4,"body":["State physiology, response, uncertainty and an urgent request.","Source-reported hip dislocation is an orthopaedic urgency; escalate, do not reduce independently.","General surgery, orthopaedics and urology coordinate; double set-up is senior-led."],"sourceDocumentIds":["SRC_SLIDES","SRC_PLAN","SRC_HANDOUT"],"contentVersion":"ptd-minigame-focused-2026-10-09"}],"sourceDocuments":[{"id":"SRC_SLIDES","title":"Pelvic Fracture for Medical Student (2024)","href":"/resources/pelvic-fracture-medical-student-2024.pdf","language":"English","note":"Supplied CNMI teaching slides by Sorawut Thamyongkit."},{"id":"SRC_PLAN","title":"Pelvic Injury Teaching Plan","href":"/resources/pelvic-injury-teaching-plan-th.pdf","language":"Thai","note":"Supplied course plan listing objectives, pre-class preparation and specialist consultation."},{"id":"SRC_HANDOUT","title":"Pelvic Fracture Teaching Handout","href":"/resources/pelvic-fracture-teaching-handout-th.pdf","language":"Thai","note":"Supplied detailed teaching handout by Kulapat Chulsomlee."}],"assets":[{"id":"A10","path":"/favicon.svg","versionHash":"local-original-1","sourceUrl":null,"owner":"Course application","licensePermission":"Original neutral application symbol","reviewStatus":"approved","reviewer":null,"reviewDate":null,"altText":"Abstract pelvic-ring application mark","caption":"Pelvic Trauma Decisions","optional":false,"downloadBytes":790},{"id":"A11","path":"/assets/student-avatar.png","versionHash":"generated-original-1","sourceUrl":null,"owner":"Course application","licensePermission":"Original AI-generated decorative character; not clinical evidence","reviewStatus":"approved","reviewer":null,"reviewDate":null,"altText":"Cartoon clinical-year medical student holding a clipboard","caption":"Learner character","optional":false,"downloadBytes":1468000},{"id":"A12","path":"/assets/faculty-mahidol.png","versionHash":"supplied-slide-crop-1","sourceUrl":null,"owner":"Mahidol University","licensePermission":"Supplied in faculty teaching slides; institutional reuse confirmation required before release","reviewStatus":"pending","reviewer":null,"reviewDate":null,"altText":"Mahidol University mark","caption":"Faculty branding from supplied teaching material","optional":false,"downloadBytes":55000},{"id":"A13","path":"/assets/cnmi.png","versionHash":"supplied-slide-crop-1","sourceUrl":null,"owner":"CNMI Ramathibodi Orthopaedic Surgery","licensePermission":"Supplied in faculty teac